{"tool_name":"metacrop","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"metacrop","home":"http://metacrop.ipk-gatersleben.de/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Database that summarizes diverse information about metabolic pathways in crop plants and allows automatic export of information for the creation of detailed metabolic models.","addition_date":"2017-03-30T23:01:05Z","last_update_date":"2019-09-18T18:31:12Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics","JIB.tools"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metacrop","credit":[{"email":"schreibe@ipk-gatersleben.de","name":"Falk Schreiber","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://metacrop.ipk-gatersleben.de/apex/f?p=269:2::::::"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics","bjsommer"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Database comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3561"},{"term":"ID mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3282"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2429"},{"term":"Metabolic labeling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3715"},{"term":"Metabolic network modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3660"}]}],"name":"MetaCrop","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkr1004","metadata":{"abstract":"MetaCrop is a manually curated repository of high-quality data about plant metabolism, providing different levels of detail from overview maps of primary metabolism to kinetic data of enzymes. It contains information about seven major crop plants with high agronomical importance and two model plants. MetaCrop is intended to support research aimed at the improvement of crops for both nutrition and industrial use. It can be accessed via web, web services and an add-on to the Vanted software. Here, we present several novel developments of the MetaCrop sy